<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- For the osacompile applets. Notarization requires the hardened
	     runtime, and the hardened runtime stops an app from ASKING to send
	     Apple events unless it holds this entitlement.

	     The failure is subtle, which is why this file exists. On a Mac that
	     already granted the app Automation, everything keeps working after
	     notarization and nothing looks wrong. On a fresh Mac (a new machine,
	     or anyone you send the app to) the app cannot prompt, so it fails
	     with "Not authorized to send Apple events" (error 1743) and never
	     appears in the Automation list for the user to switch on. There is
	     no way out of that from the receiving end.

	     Verified on macOS 26 (2026-08-15) with two otherwise identical
	     signed applets: without this key the event was refused, with it the
	     event went through.

	     NOTE TO ANYONE EDITING THIS FILE: XML comments cannot contain a
	     double hyphen. AMFI rejects the whole file with "syntax error" and
	     codesign then refuses to sign, so use commas or parentheses.

	     Nothing else belongs here. The CPython keys in pixpro.entitlements
	     (JIT, unsigned executable memory, library validation) are for the
	     py2app based apps and are meaningless to an applet. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
